<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Arab Federation</h1><p class="st-meta">1958 CE – 1958 CE · capital Baghdad</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A union of the two Hashemite kingdoms, Iraq and Jordan, formed in February 1958 as a rival to Nasser's United Arab Republic and lasting under six months.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 1 February 1958 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a> merged into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/united-arab-republic">United Arab Republic</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gamal-abdel-nasser">Gamal Abdel Nasser</a>. In response, the Hashemite cousins King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faisal-ii-of-iraq">Faisal II</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-iraq">Kingdom of Iraq</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussein-of-jordan">King Hussein</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hashemite-kingdom-of-jordan">Hashemite Kingdom of Jordan</a> proclaimed the Arab Federation on 14 February 1958.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faisal-ii-of-iraq">Faisal II</a> was head of state with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussein-of-jordan">Hussein</a> as his deputy, and each kingdom kept its own monarch and much of its own government. A federal parliament, joint army and common foreign policy were planned, and the capital was to alternate between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amman">Amman</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuri-al-said">Nuri al-Said</a> became federal prime minister. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq's</a> oil wealth was expected to support <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hashemite-kingdom-of-jordan">Jordan</a>, which had lost British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subsidy">subsidies</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 14 July 1958 the Iraqi monarchy was overthrown and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faisal-ii-of-iraq">Faisal II</a> killed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussein-of-jordan">Hussein</a> formally dissolved the federation on 2 August 1958, and the new <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-iraq">Republic of Iraq</a> withdrew from it.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/arab-federation.jpg" alt="Arab Federation" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Orange Tuesday · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Arab_Federation.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1958 CE – 1958 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Baghdad</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Faisal II, Hussein of Jordan, Nuri al-Said</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni and Shia Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a>, <a href="/countries/jordan">Jordan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Arab Federation of Iraq and Jordan, Arab Union</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1958&amp;focus=arab-federation" aria-label="Arab Federation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5814 968 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Arab Federation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6134 1224L6134 1224"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6134 1224h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6134 1224h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6134 1224h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Baghdad. <a href="/atlas?year=1958&amp;focus=arab-federation">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

